  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Embarking on a multi-room renovation is an exciting journey, and understanding the timeline involved can help you prepare. Generally, the design process for a multi-room project is quite a bit more involved than a single room. You're looking at about four to six months just for the design phase, according to experts like Houzz. This allows for creating that essential master plan for your whole home, making sure all the rooms work together seamlessly. Once the design is locked in, the construction phase can take up to three months, or even longer for larger homes. This period involves coordinating multiple trades, ordering materials, and executing the physical work. It's also super smart to factor in a contingency period – we recommend adding at least two months for unexpected surprises. Things can pop up during demolition, or material shipments can get delayed, so having that buffer is crucial. Planning for these stages helps manage expectations and keeps the project on track. When you're coordinating so many moving parts, especially if different rooms share electrical or HVAC systems, having experienced professionals like HH Remodeling LLC, who serve the greater Denver area, manage the schedule and execution can be incredibly beneficial. We help keep everything flowing smoothly."
    }
  ],
